WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.170
A house in cross-section.

2
00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:06.000
On the third storey, a young
woman paces a corridor.

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:11.160
Her speech fills the air: women
"suffer from too rigid a restraint,

4
00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.720
too absolute a stagnation".

5
00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.720
Then, from behind a door
off that same corridor,

6
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.970
a laugh: "the same low, slow ha!

7
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.070
ha!"

8
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.670
One woman gets a speech;
the other, a laugh.

9
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.140
So who speaks here, and
who is spoken about?

10
00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:31.500
In this mission, you'll meet
feminist criticism in outline,

11
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.970
and the questions it asks of a novel.

12
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:39.000
You'll read Jane's protest closely, right
up to the moment the laugh breaks in.

13
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.700
And you'll watch two critics read that
same moment in very different ways.

14
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.660
Your mission: work out who gets to speak,

15
00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.280
and who is spoken about.
